// config/base.json5 — all-agent shared behavior
//
// Layer 1/3 of the config tree. This file is $include'd by every environment
// overlay (env/host-mac.json5, env/docker.json5) and therefore reaches every
// agent: admin Mac Her + every Docker carher-{N}.
//
// Scope: fields whose value is truly identical across all 3 environments.
// Classified by the Phase 1 diagnostic as "base" (66 fields, see commit msg).
//
// What goes here:
//   - agents.defaults.compaction / memorySearch / userTimezone / llm / maxConcurrent
//   - browser.enabled / defaultProfile / cdpPortRangeStart
//   - channels.feishu.enabled / groups
//   - gateway.mode / port          (NOT bind/auth — those differ per env)
//   - messages.ackReactionScope / tts shared settings
//   - plugins.entries.* functional toggles and config that every agent needs
//   - plugins.deny
//   - tools.sessions.visibility / tools.web.search.provider
//   - Model ALIASES that every agent uses (but not per-provider apiKeys/models)
//
// What does NOT go here:
//   - Any secret or apiKey (use ${VAR_NAME} in the overlay that needs it)
//   - Environment-specific fields (gateway.bind, browser.headless, auth token)
//   - Per-user identity (feishu appId/secret, primary model)
//   - plugins.load.paths — path differs between Docker (cwd=/app) and host
//
// Array-field rule: arrays in this file MUST NOT be duplicated in any overlay.
// Deep-merge concatenates arrays, so redeclaring an array in an overlay
// appends, not replaces. To "replace", model the data as an object keyed by id.

{
}
